BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//SHAPI//API change deadlines//EN
CALSCALE:GREGORIAN
X-WR-CALNAME:SHAPI API change deadlines
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quickbooks-minorversion-below-75-ignored@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20250801T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20250801
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20250802
SUMMARY:QuickBooks Online: Minor versions below 75 are silently answered as
  minor version 75
DESCRIPTION:Since 2025-08-01 the QuickBooks Online Accounting API ignores a
 ny minorversion below 75 and responds with minor version 75 data\, without
  an error. Code pinned to an older minor version receives a different resp
 onse shape with no signal.\n\nWhat to do: Set minorversion=75 (or remove i
 t) and re-test parsing against minor version 75 responses.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/quickbooks-minorversion-below-75-ignored
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:hubspot-marketing-emails-v1-sunset@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20251101T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20251101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20251102
SUMMARY:HubSpot: Marketing Email API v1 sunset on 2025-11-01
DESCRIPTION:HubSpot sunset the v1 Marketing Email API (/marketing-emails/v1
 /...) on 2025-11-01 in favour of the Marketing Email v3 API\; requests to 
 v1 after that date return an error. Other legacy email APIs\, including em
 ail analytics\, are not affected. HubSpot's changelog post is now a 404\, 
 so the source is its Wayback Machine copy.\n\nWhat to do: Move email calls
  from /marketing-emails/v1/emails to the Marketing Email v3 API (POST /mar
 keting/v3/emails to create\, GET /marketing/v3/emails to list\, GET /marke
 ting/v3/emails/{emailId} to read one) and read folders from folderIdV2: fo
 lderId was removed from v3 on 2026-01-28. Other legacy email APIs\, such a
 s email analytics\, are not part of this sunset.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/hubspot-marketing-emails-v1-sunset
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:meta-graph-instagram-oembed-fields-removed@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20251103T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20251103
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20251104
SUMMARY:Meta Graph API: oEmbed responses no longer return author and thumbn
 ail fields
DESCRIPTION:Since 2025-11-03\, on all API versions\, Instagram post oEmbed 
 responses (GET /{version}/instagram_oembed) no longer include author_name\
 , author_url\, thumbnail_url\, thumbnail_width or thumbnail_height. The sa
 me fields were removed from Facebook post and video oEmbed (oembed_post\, 
 oembed_video)\, and the Facebook page oEmbed endpoint was deprecated.\n\nW
 hat to do: Stop reading author and thumbnail fields from oEmbed and render
  the returned html instead. If you need a thumbnail or author\, read them 
 from the Instagram Graph API media object for media your app can access\, 
 and treat the oEmbed fields as absent.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/meta-graph-instagram-oembed-fields-removed
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:slack-files-upload-retired@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20251112T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20251112
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20251113
SUMMARY:Slack: files.upload Web API method sunset on 2025-11-12
DESCRIPTION:Slack deprecated files.upload. Apps created on or after 2024-05
 -16 could not use it\, and Slack's reference page says the method stops wo
 rking and is sunset on 2025-11-12 for existing apps too (the date was move
 d from 2025-03-11). Code that still uploads through files.upload fails wit
 h method_deprecated or deprecated_endpoint errors.\n\nWhat to do: Replace 
 files.upload with the two-step flow: call files.getUploadURLExternal (file
 name\, length) to get an upload_url and file_id\, POST the file bytes to u
 pload_url\, then call files.completeUploadExternal with the file_id(s) and
  the channel_id\, initial_comment or thread_ts you used to pass to files.u
 pload. The official Slack SDKs wrap this as files_upload_v2 / filesUploadV
 2 / uploadV2.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/slack-files-upload-retired
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:meta-graph-page-insights-impressions-fans-removed@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20251115T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20251115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20251116
SUMMARY:Meta Graph API: Page Insights impressions and page fans metrics rem
 oved on 2025-11-15
DESCRIPTION:Since 2025-11-15\, on all API versions\, requesting the Page an
 d post impressions metrics (page_impressions\, page_impressions_paid\, pag
 e_impressions_viral\, page_impressions_nonviral\, post_impressions\, post_
 impressions_paid\, post_impressions_fan\, post_impressions_organic\, post_
 impressions_viral\, post_impressions_nonviral) or the fans metrics (page_f
 ans\, page_fans_locale\, page_fans_city\, page_fans_country\, page_fan_add
 s\, page_fan_adds_unique\, page_fan_removes\, page_fan_removes_unique) ret
 urns an invalid metric error. SHAPI flags calls that request one of these 
 metrics.\n\nWhat to do: Replace page_impressions with page_media_view and 
 post_impressions with post_media_view (use the is_from_ads or is_from_foll
 owers breakdowns for the paid\, organic and fan splits)\, and replace page
 _fans/page_fans_city/page_fans_country with page_follows/page_follows_city
 /page_follows_country. Remove the other listed metrics\; one invalid metri
 c fails the whole insights request.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/meta-graph-page-insights-impressions-fans-
 removed
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:github-workflow-dispatch-204-to-200@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20251219T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20251219
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20251220
SUMMARY:GitHub: workflow_dispatch returns 200 with a body instead of 204
DESCRIPTION:POST .../actions/workflows/{workflow_id}/dispatches started ans
 wering 200 OK with a JSON body (workflow run id) instead of 204 No Content
 . The OpenAPI schema and docs still said 204\, and there was no changelog\
 , version\, or preview header. Clients that require exactly 204 treat a su
 ccessful dispatch as a failure. GitHub later (2026-02-19) documented 200 a
 s the response when return_run_details is set\, and GitHub CLI v2.87.0+ se
 ts it by default.\n\nWhat to do: Treat both 200 and 204 as success (any 2x
 x). If you want the run id\, send return_run_details: true and read it fro
 m the 200 body.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/github-workflow-dispatch-204-to-200
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quickbooks-companyinfo-neoenabled-removed@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20260127T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260127
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260128
SUMMARY:QuickBooks Online: CompanyInfo no longer returns the NeoEnabled Nam
 eValue
DESCRIPTION:Since 2026-01-27 in production (2025-12-10 in sandbox)\, the Co
 mpanyInfo entity no longer includes the NeoEnabled attribute in its NameVa
 lue list. Code that looks up NeoEnabled gets no entry\, while the API refe
 rence samples still show it.\n\nWhat to do: Treat a missing NeoEnabled ent
 ry in CompanyInfo.NameValue as normal\, and stop deciding behavior from it
 . The same applies to CompanyInfo returned by the query endpoint.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/quickbooks-companyinfo-neoenabled-removed
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:hubspot-marketing-emails-folderid-removed@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20260128T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260128
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260129
SUMMARY:HubSpot: Marketing Email v3 stopped returning folderId on 2026-01-2
 8
DESCRIPTION:HubSpot moved marketing email folders to a v2 folder system and
  added folderIdV2 to Marketing Email v3 responses. Both fields were return
 ed side by side until folderId was removed on 2026-01-28\; since then only
  folderIdV2 is returned\, so code keyed on folderId gets no folder value.\
 n\nWhat to do: Read folderIdV2 instead of folderId from /marketing/v3/emai
 ls responses and re-key any stored folder index on folderIdV2 (list emails
  with folderId__not_null to rebuild it)\; old folderId values no longer ma
 tch anything the API returns.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/hubspot-marketing-emails-folderid-removed
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:shopify-delivery-method-definition-rate-groups@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20260224T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260224
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260225
SUMMARY:Shopify: Shopify shipping options move to rateGroups\; rateProvider
  and methodConditions are legacy
DESCRIPTION:A shipping option can now hold several tiered rates. DeliveryMe
 thodDefinition.rateGroups and DeliveryRateDefinition.conditions replace th
 e legacy rateProvider and methodConditions fields\, and apps that write me
 rchant-managed delivery profiles must move to the new write API.\n\nWhat t
 o do: Read shipping options from DeliveryMethodDefinition.rateGroups and D
 eliveryRateDefinition.conditions\, and use the new write API for merchant-
 managed delivery profiles\; app-managed profiles need no change.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/shopify-delivery-method-definition-rate-gr
 oups
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:x-activity-api-pascalcase-event-types-removed@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20260318T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260318
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260319
SUMMARY:X (Twitter): X Activity API event types renamed from PascalCase to 
 dot-separated lowercase
DESCRIPTION:From 2026-03-18 the X Activity API (XAA) uses dot-separated low
 ercase event_type values such as profile.update.bio instead of PascalCase 
 names such as ProfileBioUpdate. Subscriptions created with\, or event hand
 lers that switch on\, the old names stop matching.\n\nWhat to do: Send the
  new lowercase names (for example profile.update.bio\, follow.follow\, pos
 t.create) in POST /2/activity/subscriptions and update every filter\, swit
 ch statement and deserializer that reads event_type from the activity stre
 am or webhook payloads.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/x-activity-api-pascalcase-event-types-remo
 ved
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:shopify-rest-order-line-item-pre-tax-price-removed@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20260323T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260323
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260324
SUMMARY:Shopify: Shopify removes pre_tax_price from REST order line items
DESCRIPTION:The pre_tax_price and pre_tax_price_set fields on order line it
 ems in the REST Admin API are removed. They were only populated for stores
  using the Avalara AvaTax 1.0 integration\, deprecated in April 2025.\n\nW
 hat to do: Read order line item pricing from the GraphQL Admin API instead
  of pre_tax_price.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/shopify-rest-order-line-item-pre-tax-price
 -removed
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stripe-checkout-session-ui-mode-values-renamed@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20260325T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260325
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260326
SUMMARY:Stripe: Stripe 2026-03-25.dahlia renames Checkout Session ui_mode v
 alues
DESCRIPTION:From API version 2026-03-25.dahlia\, Checkout Session ui_mode v
 alues hosted\, embedded and custom are replaced by hosted_page\, embedded_
 page and elements (and form is added). Creating a session with an old valu
 e fails\, and code that compares the returned ui_mode to the old strings s
 tops matching once the account or SDK is upgraded.\n\nWhat to do: When mov
 ing to 2026-03-25.dahlia or later\, send ui_mode hosted_page instead of ho
 sted\, embedded_page instead of embedded and elements instead of custom\, 
 and update every comparison of session.ui_mode (including checkout.session
  webhook handlers) to the new values\; handle the new form value too.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/stripe-checkout-session-ui-mode-values-ren
 amed
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:shopify-inventory-activate-preserves-quantities@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20260401T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260401
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260402
SUMMARY:Shopify: Shopify inventoryActivate keeps existing quantities instea
 d of resetting them to zero\, as of 2026-04
DESCRIPTION:As of Admin API version 2026-04\, inventoryActivate without an 
 available or onHand argument keeps an inventory level's earlier quantities
  instead of resetting them to zero.\n\nWhat to do: Pass available or onHan
 d explicitly to inventoryActivate if your app relied on activation resetti
 ng quantities to zero.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/shopify-inventory-activate-preserves-quant
 ities
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:shopify-rest-inventory-connect-preserves-quantities@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20260401T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260401
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260402
SUMMARY:Shopify: Shopify's REST inventory_levels/connect keeps existing qua
 ntities instead of resetting them\, as of 2026-04
DESCRIPTION:As of Admin API version 2026-04\, POST inventory_levels/connect
 .json keeps an inventory level's earlier quantities instead of resetting t
 hem to zero.\n\nWhat to do: Set the available quantity explicitly after co
 nnecting a location if your app relied on it starting at zero.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/shopify-rest-inventory-connect-preserves-q
 uantities
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:x-self-serve-follow-writes-removed@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20260416T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260416
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260417
SUMMARY:X (Twitter): Following users removed from X API self-serve tiers
DESCRIPTION:X's 2026-04-16 changelog says Following via the API has been re
 moved from all self-serve tiers (Free\, Basic\, Pro\, pay-per-use)\, leavi
 ng it to Enterprise. POST /2/users/{id}/following calls with self-serve cr
 edentials are rejected\; X does not document the status code.\n\nWhat to d
 o: Remove or feature-flag follow actions for self-serve apps and show user
 s a clear message (for example a link to the profile so they can follow in
  the X app)\, or move to an Enterprise agreement.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/x-self-serve-follow-writes-removed
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:x-self-serve-like-writes-removed@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20260416T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260416
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260417
SUMMARY:X (Twitter): Liking Posts removed from X API self-serve tiers
DESCRIPTION:X's 2026-04-16 changelog says Following\, Likes and Quote-Posts
  via the API have been removed from all self-serve tiers (Free\, Basic\, P
 ro\, pay-per-use)\, leaving them to Enterprise. POST /2/users/{id}/likes c
 alls with self-serve credentials are rejected\; X does not document the st
 atus code. Quote-Posts (POST /2/tweets with quote_tweet_id) are also remov
 ed but cannot be matched by path.\n\nWhat to do: Remove or feature-flag li
 ke actions for self-serve apps and surface a clear error to users\, or mov
 e to an Enterprise agreement. Also drop quote_tweet_id from POST /2/tweets
  on self-serve keys.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/x-self-serve-like-writes-removed
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:shopify-order-transaction-total-unsettled-fixed@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20260424T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260424
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260425
SUMMARY:Shopify: Shopify fixes OrderTransaction.totalUnsettledSet for pendi
 ng captures
DESCRIPTION:OrderTransaction.totalUnsettledSet no longer double-counts a pe
 nding capture: for a $100 authorization with a $50 pending capture it retu
 rns $100\, not $150. The fix applies to all API versions at once and only 
 affects multi-capture orders.\n\nWhat to do: Check any logic that compensa
 ted for the inflated totalUnsettledSet on multi-capture orders\; the field
  now returns the amount still capturable.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/shopify-order-transaction-total-unsettled-
 fixed
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:hubspot-contact-lists-v1-sunset@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20260430T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260430
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260501
SUMMARY:HubSpot: Contact Lists API v1 retired on 2026-04-30\; endpoints ret
 urn 404
DESCRIPTION:HubSpot sunset the v1 Contact Lists API on 2026-04-30 (moved fr
 om 2025-09-30). Since then the /contacts/v1/lists endpoints for creating\,
  updating\, deleting and reading lists and list contacts return HTTP 404. 
 The replacement is the Lists API (2026-03 or v3)\, which uses a new listId
  instead of the v1 legacyListId.\n\nWhat to do: Map each stored legacyList
 Id to the new listId with GET /crm/lists/2026-03/idmapping?legacyListId=..
 . (or POST /crm/lists/2026-03/idmapping for up to 10\,000 ids\; ids in mis
 singLegacyListIds no longer exist)\, then move reads to GET /crm/lists/202
 6-03/{listId} and /crm/lists/2026-03/{listId}/memberships\, and membership
  writes to PUT /crm/lists/2026-03/{listId}/memberships/add\, /remove or /a
 dd-and-remove. The legacy GET /v1/lists/{legacyListId}/sizeAndEditsHistory
 /between endpoint was retired too and is not covered by this path pattern.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/hubspot-contact-lists-v1-sunset
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:hubspot-contacts-v1-list-memberships-removed@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20260430T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260430
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260501
SUMMARY:HubSpot: v1 contact read endpoints stopped returning list membershi
 ps on 2026-04-30
DESCRIPTION:With the Contact Lists v1 sunset\, six v1 contact read endpoint
 s (get by vid\, email or utk\, and their batch versions) keep working but\
 , since 2026-04-30\, no longer return list memberships. The field in the v
 1 response is list-memberships (requested with showListMemberships)\; code
  that reads it now gets no membership data\, without an error.\n\nWhat to 
 do: Stop reading list-memberships from /contacts/v1/contact/... responses.
  Map stored legacy list ids to new list ids with /crm/lists/2026-03/idmapp
 ing\, then read list members from GET /crm/lists/2026-03/{listId}/membersh
 ips (results ordered by record id) and build the contact-to-list mapping f
 rom that\, or move contact reads to the current CRM objects API together w
 ith the Lists API.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/hubspot-contacts-v1-list-memberships-remov
 ed
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:xero-finance-accounting-activities-decommissioned@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260504
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260505
SUMMARY:Xero: Finance API Accounting Activities endpoints decommissioned
DESCRIPTION:On 2026-05-04 Xero decommissioned the Finance API's Accounting 
 Activities API: Account Usage\, Lock History\, Report History and User Act
 ivities. All of these endpoints now return errors. Xero suggests the Bank 
 Statements API for cash flow and financial analysis.\n\nWhat to do: Remove
  calls to /finance.xro/1.0/AccountingActivities/AccountUsage\, LockHistory
 \, ReportHistory and UserActivities\, along with the features built on the
 m. For cash-flow or transaction analysis\, move to the Finance API Bank St
 atements endpoint (/finance.xro/1.0/BankStatementsPlus/statements). Lock h
 istory and user activity data have no direct replacement.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/xero-finance-accounting-activities-decommi
 ssioned
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:reddit-logged-out-json-403@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20260530T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260530
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260531
SUMMARY:Reddit: Logged-out .json endpoints return 403
DESCRIPTION:Unauthenticated requests to Reddit's public .json listing endpo
 ints (for example /r/{subreddit}/top.json) started returning 403 Forbidden
  around 2026-05-30. Reddit announced the shutdown of unauthenticated .json
  endpoints in r/modnews on 2026-05-28 and said logged-in and authenticated
  access is not affected\; the 403 status and the 2026-05-30 date come from
  third-party reports.\n\nWhat to do: Move to an approved OAuth app and cal
 l oauth.reddit.com with a bearer token. Reddit's notice points developers 
 who need structured access to Devvit.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/reddit-logged-out-json-403
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:google-gemini-2-0-flash-shutdown@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20260601T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260601
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260602
SUMMARY:Google Gemini API: gemini-2.0-flash and gemini-2.0-flash-lite shut 
 down on 2026-06-01
DESCRIPTION:Google shut down gemini-2.0-flash\, gemini-2.0-flash-001\, gemi
 ni-2.0-flash-lite and gemini-2.0-flash-lite-001 on 2026-06-01. A shut-down
  model is completely turned off\, so generateContent and streamGenerateCon
 tent calls that name it in the path fail. Calls that pass the model in a r
 equest body (as /v1beta/interactions does) or in a variable are not matche
 d by this path.\n\nWhat to do: Change the model segment to gemini-3.6-flas
 h (for gemini-2.0-flash) or gemini-3.1-flash-lite (for gemini-2.0-flash-li
 te)\, for example /v1beta/models/gemini-3.6-flash:generateContent\, and re
 -test prompts and output parsing.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/google-gemini-2-0-flash-shutdown
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:google-gemini-2-0-flash-shutdown-sdk@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20260601T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260601
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260602
SUMMARY:Google Gemini API: gemini-2.0-flash and gemini-2.0-flash-lite shut 
 down on 2026-06-01 (model in the request body)
DESCRIPTION:Google shut down gemini-2.0-flash\, gemini-2.0-flash-001\, gemi
 ni-2.0-flash-lite and gemini-2.0-flash-lite-001 on 2026-06-01. A shut-down
  model is completely turned off\, so generateContent and streamGenerateCon
 tent calls fail. This advisory covers calls that pass the model as a param
 eter\, as the @google/genai SDK does (ai.models.generateContent({ model })
 )\; google-gemini-2-0-flash-shutdown covers calls that name the model in t
 he path.\n\nWhat to do: Change the model to gemini-3.6-flash (for gemini-2
 .0-flash) or gemini-3.1-flash-lite (for gemini-2.0-flash-lite)\, and re-te
 st prompts and output parsing.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/google-gemini-2-0-flash-shutdown-sdk
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:meta-graph-page-insights-reach-video-views-removed@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20260615T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260615
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260616
SUMMARY:Meta Graph API: Page Insights reach and 3-second video viewer metri
 cs removed on 2026-06-15
DESCRIPTION:By 2026-06-15\, on all API versions\, the Page/post reach metri
 cs (page_impressions_unique\, post_impressions_unique and their paid\, vir
 al\, nonviral\, organic and fan variants\, the page_posts_impressions fami
 ly\, page_posts_served_impressions_organic_unique) and the 3-second viewer
  metrics (page_video_views_unique\, post_video_views_unique) return an inv
 alid metric error. SHAPI flags calls that request one of these metrics.\n\
 nWhat to do: Switch reach and unique-viewer reporting to page_total_media_
 view_unique and post_total_media_view_unique (and page_media_view/post_med
 ia_view with is_from_ads for paid vs organic). The numbers use a different
  method\, so do not splice them onto historical reach series\, and drop me
 trics that have no replacement (viral/nonviral reach).
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/meta-graph-page-insights-reach-video-views
 -removed
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:xero-organisation-class-ultra-enum@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20260630T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260630
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260701
SUMMARY:Xero: Organisation Class enum gains ULTRA
DESCRIPTION:Since 2026-06-30 the Organisation endpoint can return Class ULT
 RA for Australian organisations on the new Xero Ultra plan. Xero warns tha
 t integrations assuming only the existing values may fail to keep their co
 nnection to Xero. Strict enum parsing\, including older SDK enums\, can th
 row on the new value.\n\nWhat to do: Accept unknown Organisation Class val
 ues instead of failing\, and map ULTRA wherever you branch on plan type. I
 f you use a generated SDK\, upgrade to a version whose Class enum includes
  ULTRA\, or deserialize Class as a plain string.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/xero-organisation-class-ultra-enum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:shopify-customer-payment-method-remote-create-identifier-required@shapi
 .dev
DTSTAMP:20260701T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260701
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260702
SUMMARY:Shopify: Shopify customerPaymentMethodRemoteCreate requires a payme
 nt method identifier as of 2026-07
DESCRIPTION:As of Admin API version 2026-07\, customerPaymentMethodRemoteCr
 eate requires the gateway's payment method identifier: paymentMethodId for
  Stripe\, customerPaymentProfileId for Authorize.net\, paymentMethodToken 
 for Braintree.\n\nWhat to do: Send the gateway's payment method identifier
  with every customerPaymentMethodRemoteCreate call before moving to 2026-0
 7.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/shopify-customer-payment-method-remote-cre
 ate-identifier-required
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:shopify-inventory-set-scheduled-changes-removed@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20260701T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260701
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260702
SUMMARY:Shopify: Shopify removes the inventorySetScheduledChanges mutation 
 in API version 2026-07
DESCRIPTION:As of Admin API version 2026-07\, the inventorySetScheduledChan
 ges mutation is removed with no replacement.\n\nWhat to do: Remove calls t
 o inventorySetScheduledChanges. Use inventoryAdjustQuantities for immediat
 e adjustments\, or schedule changes in your own app.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/shopify-inventory-set-scheduled-changes-re
 moved
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:twilio-voice-insights-conference-participant-removed@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20260801T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260801
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260802
SUMMARY:Twilio: Twilio Voice Insights Call Summary drops attributes.confere
 nce_participant on 2026-08-01
DESCRIPTION:On August 1\, 2026 Twilio removed the conference_participant at
 tribute from the Voice Insights Call Summary (GET /v1/Voice/{CallSid}/Summ
 ary on insights.twilio.com) and the matching Event Streams event\; attribu
 tes now returns null for every call. Code that reads attributes.conference
 _participant gets nothing\, and code that dereferences attributes can thro
 w.\n\nWhat to do: Stop reading attributes.conference_participant and treat
  attributes as nullable. Get conference data from the Conference Insights 
 API or Conference Insights Event Streams instead.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/twilio-voice-insights-conference-participa
 nt-removed
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:twilio-rcs-undelivered-error-code-30046@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20260810T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260810
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260811
SUMMARY:Twilio: Twilio RCS unconfirmed-delivery error code changed from 300
 36 to 30046
DESCRIPTION:Since August 10\, 2026\, an RCS message that cannot be delivere
 d to an unreachable device fails with error code 30046 (Message delivery n
 ot confirmed) instead of 30036 (Validity Period Expired). Custom SMS failo
 ver logic that checks error_code or ErrorCode for 30036 no longer fires\; 
 Twilio's native SMS fallback is not affected.\n\nWhat to do: Wherever you 
 branch on error_code (Message resource\; errorCode in the Node.js SDK) or 
 ErrorCode (status callbacks) to trigger SMS failover for RCS\, treat 30046
  the same as 30036\, and test the fallback path.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/twilio-rcs-undelivered-error-code-30046
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:openai-assistants-api-shutdown@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20260826T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260826
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260827
SUMMARY:OpenAI: Assistants API removed on 2026-08-26
DESCRIPTION:OpenAI removed the Assistants API on 2026-08-26\, one year afte
 r its 2025-08-26 deprecation notice. Calls to the assistants endpoints\, a
 nd to the threads\, messages and runs endpoints that go with them (/v1/thr
 eads/**)\, no longer work. The replacement is the Responses API plus the C
 onversations API.\n\nWhat to do: Move assistants to prompts (configuration
  created in the dashboard)\, threads to Conversations\, and runs to Respon
 ses (send input items or a conversation id to the Responses API)\, and run
  the tool-call loop in your own code. Thread messages can no longer be fet
 ched from the API\, so read history from your own stored copy.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/openai-assistants-api-shutdown
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:openai-assistants-threads-api-shutdown@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20260826T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260826
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260827
SUMMARY:OpenAI: Assistants API threads\, messages and runs removed on 2026-
 08-26
DESCRIPTION:OpenAI removed the Assistants API on 2026-08-26\, one year afte
 r its 2025-08-26 deprecation notice\, including the threads\, messages and
  runs endpoints that go with it (/v1/threads/**). Calls to them no longer 
 work. The replacement is the Responses API plus the Conversations API. The
  assistants endpoints themselves are covered by openai-assistants-api-shut
 down.\n\nWhat to do: Move assistants to prompts (configuration created in 
 the dashboard)\, threads to Conversations\, and runs to Responses (send in
 put items or a conversation id to the Responses API)\, and run the tool-ca
 ll loop in your own code. Thread messages can no longer be fetched from th
 e API\, so read history from your own stored copy.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/openai-assistants-threads-api-shutdown
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:xero-au-payroll-isqualifyingearnings-required@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20260910T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260910
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260911
SUMMARY:Xero: AU Payroll pay item and earnings rate writes require IsQualif
 yingEarnings
DESCRIPTION:Since 2026-09-10\, AU Payroll create and update requests for Ea
 rnings Rates and Pay Items must include IsQualifyingEarnings. Requests wit
 hout it return a 400 validation error\, and when it is true the matching s
 uper flag must agree. The same rule applies to the v2 endpoint POST /payro
 ll.xro/2.0/earningsRates.\n\nWhat to do: Add IsQualifyingEarnings to every
  earnings rate sent to POST /payroll.xro/1.0/PayItems\, and isQualifyingEa
 rnings to POST /payroll.xro/2.0/earningsRates. Keep it consistent with the
  super flags: when it is true\, Pay Items need IsExemptFromSuper false and
  Earnings Rates need IsSubjectToSuper true. For rates you read and write b
 ack\, keep the value Xero returned.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/xero-au-payroll-isqualifyingearnings-requi
 red
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:xero-au-payroll-isqualifyingearnings-required-earningsrates@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20260910T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260910
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260911
SUMMARY:Xero: AU Payroll pay item and earnings rate writes require IsQualif
 yingEarnings (v2 earningsRates)
DESCRIPTION:Since 2026-09-10\, AU Payroll create and update requests for Ea
 rnings Rates and Pay Items must include IsQualifyingEarnings. Requests wit
 hout it return a 400 validation error\, and when it is true the matching s
 uper flag must agree. This advisory covers the v2 endpoint POST /payroll.x
 ro/2.0/earningsRates\; xero-au-payroll-isqualifyingearnings-required cover
 s POST /payroll.xro/1.0/PayItems.\n\nWhat to do: Add IsQualifyingEarnings 
 to every earnings rate sent to POST /payroll.xro/1.0/PayItems\, and isQual
 ifyingEarnings to POST /payroll.xro/2.0/earningsRates. Keep it consistent 
 with the super flags: when it is true\, Pay Items need IsExemptFromSuper f
 alse and Earnings Rates need IsSubjectToSuper true. For rates you read and
  write back\, keep the value Xero returned.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/xero-au-payroll-isqualifyingearnings-requi
 red-earningsrates
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:meta-graph-v20-sunset@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20260924T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260924
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260925
SUMMARY:Meta Graph API: Graph API v20.0 removed\; calls fall forward to the
  next version
DESCRIPTION:Graph API v20.0 was deprecated and removed on 2026-09-24. Calls
  pinned to v20.0 do not fail: they are served by the next oldest usable ve
 rsion\, so response shapes can change silently.\n\nWhat to do: Move the ve
 rsion segment to a supported version (v22.0 or later) and re-test the fiel
 ds you read.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/meta-graph-v20-sunset
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stripe-endive-billing-cycle-anchor-object@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20260930T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Stripe: Stripe 2026-09-30.endive requires an object for billing_cyc
 le_anchor on subscription updates
DESCRIPTION:From API version 2026-09-30.endive\, billing_cycle_anchor on Su
 bscription update and resume (and subscription_details.billing_cycle_ancho
 r on Invoice create_preview) takes an object with a type instead of the st
 rings now and unchanged\, so requests sending the old string form fail.\n\
 nWhat to do: When moving to 2026-09-30.endive\, send billing_cycle_anchor:
  {type: 'now'} instead of 'now' and {type: 'unchanged'} instead of 'unchan
 ged' when updating or resuming a subscription. For a preview invoice of a 
 new subscription anchored to a timestamp\, send {type: 'timestamp'\, times
 tamp: <unix seconds>}.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/stripe-endive-billing-cycle-anchor-object
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stripe-endive-checkout-session-payment-method-types-removed@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20260930T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Stripe: Stripe 2026-09-30.endive removes payment_method_types from 
 Checkout Session creation
DESCRIPTION:From API version 2026-09-30.endive\, creating a Checkout Sessio
 n with payment_method_types returns a 400 error. Stripe replaces it with d
 ynamic payment methods\, excluded_payment_method_types\, or the new allowe
 d_payment_method_types\, which filters out incompatible types instead of f
 ailing.\n\nWhat to do: Before moving to 2026-09-30.endive\, stop sending p
 ayment_method_types when creating Checkout Sessions. Use dynamic payment m
 ethods (manage them in the Dashboard)\, excluded_payment_method_types to d
 rop some\, or allowed_payment_method_types to list the ones you accept.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/stripe-endive-checkout-session-payment-met
 hod-types-removed
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stripe-endive-payment-intent-payment-method-types-removed@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20260930T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Stripe: Stripe 2026-09-30.endive removes payment_method_types from 
 Payment Intent create\, update and confirm
DESCRIPTION:From API version 2026-09-30.endive\, payment_method_types is no
  longer writable on Payment Intents: create\, update and confirm requests 
 that send it return a 400 error. It stays a read-only property on the Paym
 ent Intent\, listing the computed payment methods.\n\nWhat to do: Before m
 oving to 2026-09-30.endive\, stop sending payment_method_types when creati
 ng\, updating or confirming Payment Intents. Use dynamic payment methods\,
  excluded_payment_method_types\, or allowed_payment_method_types (incompat
 ible types are filtered out instead of failing). Reading payment_method_ty
 pes from the returned object still works.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/stripe-endive-payment-intent-payment-metho
 d-types-removed
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stripe-endive-setup-intent-payment-method-types-removed@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20260930T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Stripe: Stripe 2026-09-30.endive removes payment_method_types from 
 Setup Intent create and update
DESCRIPTION:From API version 2026-09-30.endive\, payment_method_types is no
  longer writable on Setup Intents: create and update requests that send it
  return a 400 error. It stays a read-only property on the Setup Intent.\n\
 nWhat to do: Before moving to 2026-09-30.endive\, stop sending payment_met
 hod_types when creating or updating Setup Intents. Use dynamic payment met
 hods\, excluded_payment_method_types\, or allowed_payment_method_types.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/stripe-endive-setup-intent-payment-method-
 types-removed
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:twilio-conference-list-default-in-progress@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20260930T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Twilio: Twilio Conference list returns only in-progress conferences
  by default from 2026-09-30
DESCRIPTION:Starting September 30\, 2026 (rollout delayed from July 13\, 20
 26)\, GET /2010-04-01/Accounts/{AccountSid}/Conferences.json without a Sta
 tus filter returns only in-progress conferences instead of in-progress and
  completed ones. Code that lists conferences without Status and expects co
 mpleted ones gets silently incomplete results.\n\nWhat to do: Pass Status=
 completed explicitly when you need completed conferences (reporting\, bill
 ing or cleanup jobs)\, and make a second request without it for in-progres
 s ones if you need both\; do not rely on the unfiltered list containing co
 mpleted conferences.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/twilio-conference-list-default-in-progress
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:shopify-carrier-service-not-added-to-default-profile@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20261001T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Shopify: Shopify carrierServiceCreate no longer adds the carrier se
 rvice to the General shipping profile\, as of 2026-10
DESCRIPTION:As of Admin API version 2026-10\, creating a carrier service wi
 th carrierServiceCreate only registers it\; Shopify no longer adds it to t
 he General shipping profile\, so merchants see no rates from it until it i
 s added to a profile.\n\nWhat to do: After creating a carrier service\, ad
 d its rates to a shipping profile with the delivery profile APIs\, or dire
 ct merchants to add the carrier-calculated rate in the Shopify admin.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/shopify-carrier-service-not-added-to-defau
 lt-profile
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:shopify-draft-order-warning-price-rule-removed@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20261001T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Shopify: Shopify removes priceRule from DraftOrderDiscountNotApplie
 dWarning in API version 2026-10
DESCRIPTION:As of Admin API version 2026-10\, the deprecated priceRule fiel
 d on DraftOrderDiscountNotAppliedWarning (returned by draftOrderCalculate\
 , draftOrderCreate and draftOrderUpdate) is removed\, and with it the Pric
 eRule object from the public schema.\n\nWhat to do: Select discountTitle i
 nstead of priceRule { title } and discountCode instead of priceRule { disc
 ountCodes { nodes { code } } } on DraftOrderDiscountNotAppliedWarning.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/shopify-draft-order-warning-price-rule-rem
 oved
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:shopify-order-display-fulfillment-status-not-required@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20261001T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Shopify: Shopify OrderDisplayFulfillmentStatus can return FULFILLME
 NT_NOT_REQUIRED as of 2026-10
DESCRIPTION:As of Admin API version 2026-10\, Order.displayFulfillmentStatu
 s can return FULFILLMENT_NOT_REQUIRED for orders with nothing left to fulf
 ill (cancelled or refunded before fulfillment)\, which returned UNFULFILLE
 D before.\n\nWhat to do: Handle FULFILLMENT_NOT_REQUIRED wherever the code
  maps or filters displayFulfillmentStatus\, and stop treating these orders
  as UNFULFILLED.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/shopify-order-display-fulfillment-status-n
 ot-required
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:shopify-order-update-shipping-address-recalculates-taxes@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20261001T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Shopify: Shopify orderUpdate recalculates taxes when an unfulfilled
  order's shipping address changes\, as of 2026-10
DESCRIPTION:As of Admin API version 2026-10\, changing the shipping address
  of an unfulfilled order with orderUpdate recalculates its taxes and total
 s against the new destination. Before\, the tax lines were left unchanged.
 \n\nWhat to do: After updating a shipping address\, read the order's taxLi
 nes\, totalTaxSet and totals again instead of assuming they are unchanged\
 ; reconcile any amounts your app stored.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/shopify-order-update-shipping-address-reca
 lculates-taxes
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:shopify-rest-carrier-service-not-added-to-default-profile@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20261001T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Shopify: Shopify's REST carrier service creation no longer adds it 
 to the General shipping profile\, as of 2026-10
DESCRIPTION:As of Admin API version 2026-10\, POST carrier_services.json on
 ly registers the carrier service\; Shopify no longer adds it to the Genera
 l shipping profile.\n\nWhat to do: After creating a carrier service\, add 
 its rates to a shipping profile\, or direct merchants to add the carrier-c
 alculated rate in the Shopify admin.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/shopify-rest-carrier-service-not-added-to-
 default-profile
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:shopify-rest-order-update-shipping-address-recalculates-taxes@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20261001T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Shopify: Shopify's REST order update recalculates taxes when an unf
 ulfilled order's shipping address changes\, as of 2026-10
DESCRIPTION:As of Admin API version 2026-10\, changing the shipping address
  of an unfulfilled order through the REST order update endpoint recalculat
 es its taxes and totals against the new destination.\n\nWhat to do: After 
 updating a shipping address\, read the order's tax lines and totals again 
 instead of assuming they are unchanged.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/shopify-rest-order-update-shipping-address
 -recalculates-taxes
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:shopify-segment-query-function-syntax@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20261001T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Shopify: Shopify segment query functions use MATCHES instead of = t
 rue as of API version 2026-10
DESCRIPTION:As of Admin API version 2026-10\, functions in the customer seg
 ment query language use MATCHES / NOT MATCHES instead of = true / = false 
 (shopify_email.opened MATCHES ())\, function parameters take their own ope
 rators\, and the named dates 12_months_ago\, 90_days_ago\, 30_days_ago and
  7_days_ago are deprecated.\n\nWhat to do: Rewrite segment queries for 202
 6-10: replace function() = true with function MATCHES () and = false with 
 NOT MATCHES ()\, move parameters inside the parentheses (products_purchase
 d MATCHES (quantity = 5))\, and replace named dates with offsets such as -
 12m.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/shopify-segment-query-function-syntax
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:google-ads-api-v22-sunset@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20261007T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261007
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261008
SUMMARY:Google APIs: Google Ads API v22 sunset on 2026-10-07
DESCRIPTION:Google Ads API v22 was sunset on 2026-10-07\; from that date al
 l v22 requests fail. Code still pinned to /v22/ paths\, or to client libra
 ry versions that only speak v22\, is broken.\n\nWhat to do: Change the ver
 sion segment of googleads.googleapis.com paths to a supported version (v24
  or later is safest\, since v23 sunsets in February 2027)\, upgrade the cl
 ient library\, and work through each skipped version's breaking-changes li
 st. The Google Ads API metrics page in the Cloud Console shows which versi
 oned methods your project still calls.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/google-ads-api-v22-sunset
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:xero-allocations-contact-mismatch-rejected@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20261008T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261008
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261009
SUMMARY:Xero: Allocations between documents of different contacts are rejec
 ted
DESCRIPTION:Xero is beginning to require (notice of 2026-10-08) a credit no
 te\, prepayment or overpayment to belong to the same contact as the invoic
 e or bill it is allocated to. Allocation requests that create a new contac
 t mismatch return a validation error (HTTP 400). The notice is dated 2026-
 10-08 and gives no separate enforcement date.\n\nWhat to do: Before callin
 g PUT /CreditNotes/{CreditNoteID}/Allocations\, /Prepayments/{PrepaymentID
 }/Allocations or /Overpayments/{OverpaymentID}/Allocations\, check that Co
 ntact.ContactID is the same on the source document and on the target invoi
 ce or bill. On a validation error\, show the user the mismatch instead of 
 retrying\, because the unchanged request keeps failing.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/xero-allocations-contact-mismatch-rejected
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:anthropic-api-version-2026-10-21-sampling-params-400@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20261021T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Anthropic: anthropic-version 2026-10-21 rejects temperature\, top_p
  and top_k with 400
DESCRIPTION:API version 2026-10-21 (released 2026-10-21 and sent by default
  by the new major SDK versions) removes temperature\, top_p and top_k from
  the Messages API: any request that sends one of them returns 400\, even a
 t the default value. The same version also returns 400 for document blocks
  in assistant messages and for citations on user text blocks. Requests tha
 t stay on 2023-06-01 are unchanged.\n\nWhat to do: Before sending anthropi
 c-version: 2026-10-21 or upgrading to the new SDK majors (Python 2.0.0\, T
 ypeScript 1.0.0\, Go 2.0.0\, Java 3.0.0\, Ruby 2.0.0\, PHP 1.0.0\, C# 13.0
 .0)\, remove temperature\, top_p and top_k from Messages\, token-counting 
 and batch requests\, move document blocks into user messages\, and drop ci
 tations from user text blocks. If a request depends on a non-default tempe
 rature\, keep that request on 2023-06-01.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/anthropic-api-version-2026-10-21-sampling-
 params-400
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:openai-legacy-gpt-o-series-shutdown-2026-10-23@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20261023T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261023
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261024
SUMMARY:OpenAI: gpt-3.5-turbo\, gpt-4\, gpt-4-turbo\, o1\, o3-mini and o4-m
 ini shut down on 2026-10-23
DESCRIPTION:On 2026-10-23 OpenAI shuts down gpt-3.5-turbo (0125)\, gpt-4 (0
 613)\, gpt-4-1106-preview\, gpt-4-turbo\, gpt-4.1-nano\, gpt-4o-2024-05-13
 \, o1\, o1-pro\, o3-mini and o4-mini\, plus fine-tunes of gpt-3.5-turbo\, 
 gpt-4\, gpt-4.1-nano and o4-mini. Only calls that send one of these model 
 names (or their aliases) are hit\; they fail from then on.\n\nWhat to do: 
 Search request bodies and config for these model names and switch them: gp
 t-3.5-turbo and o4-mini to gpt-5.6-terra\; gpt-4\, gpt-4-1106-preview\, gp
 t-4-turbo\, gpt-4o-2024-05-13\, o1 and o3-mini to gpt-5.6-sol\; o1-pro to 
 gpt-5.6-sol with reasoning.mode: pro\; gpt-4.1-nano to gpt-5.6-luna. Re-ru
 n fine-tunes on the new base models. The same model names also stop workin
 g on the Responses and legacy Completions endpoints.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/openai-legacy-gpt-o-series-shutdown-2026-1
 0-23
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:openai-legacy-gpt-o-series-shutdown-2026-10-23-responses@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20261023T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261023
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261024
SUMMARY:OpenAI: gpt-3.5-turbo\, gpt-4\, gpt-4-turbo\, o1\, o3-mini and o4-m
 ini shut down on 2026-10-23 (Responses API)
DESCRIPTION:On 2026-10-23 OpenAI shuts down gpt-3.5-turbo (0125)\, gpt-4 (0
 613)\, gpt-4-1106-preview\, gpt-4-turbo\, gpt-4.1-nano\, gpt-4o-2024-05-13
 \, o1\, o1-pro\, o3-mini and o4-mini\, plus fine-tunes of gpt-3.5-turbo\, 
 gpt-4\, gpt-4.1-nano and o4-mini. This advisory covers calls to the Respon
 ses API (POST /v1/responses) that send one of these model names (or their 
 aliases)\; they fail from then on. openai-legacy-gpt-o-series-shutdown-202
 6-10-23 covers chat completions.\n\nWhat to do: Search request bodies and 
 config for these model names and switch them: gpt-3.5-turbo and o4-mini to
  gpt-5.6-terra\; gpt-4\, gpt-4-1106-preview\, gpt-4-turbo\, gpt-4o-2024-05
 -13\, o1 and o3-mini to gpt-5.6-sol\; o1-pro to gpt-5.6-sol with reasoning
 .mode: pro\; gpt-4.1-nano to gpt-5.6-luna. Re-run fine-tunes on the new ba
 se models. The same model names also stop working on the Responses and leg
 acy Completions endpoints.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/openai-legacy-gpt-o-series-shutdown-2026-1
 0-23-responses
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:meta-graph-commerce-order-management-removed@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20261027T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261027
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261028
SUMMARY:Meta Graph API: Commerce Order Management API removed on all versio
 ns on 2026-10-27
DESCRIPTION:Meta deprecated the Commerce Order Management API (47 endpoints
 \, including GET /{page-id}/commerce_orders and GET /{commerce-merchant-se
 ttings-id}/commerce_orders) with no replacement. Calls on v26.0+ are block
 ed since 2026-07-29\, and the endpoints are removed from all remaining ver
 sions on 2026-10-27. Order sub-resources (items\, shipments\, refunds\, ca
 ncellations\, payments\, tax_settings) by object id go too\, but only the 
 commerce_orders list edge is matched here.\n\nWhat to do: There is no repl
 acement API. Stop calling commerce_orders\, commerce_returns\, tax_setting
 s and the order\, shipment\, refund and cancellation object reads\, and ha
 ndle orders in Commerce Manager or your own order system. Guard any remain
 ing calls so the error does not break sync jobs.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/meta-graph-commerce-order-management-remov
 ed
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:meta-graph-date-format-param-removed@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20261027T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261027
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261028
SUMMARY:Meta Graph API: date_format query parameter returns an error from 2
 026-10-27
DESCRIPTION:Requests that include the legacy date_format parameter return a
 n error on Graph API v26.0+ since 2026-07-29 and on all supported versions
  from 2026-10-27. The same change makes pretty and debug ignored and remov
 es ETag/304 Not Modified behaviour.\n\nWhat to do: Remove date_format from
  every Graph API request and parse the default ISO 8601 timestamps in your
  own code. While you are there\, drop any reliance on If-None-Match/304 ca
 ching and on pretty or debug output.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/meta-graph-date-format-param-removed
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:meta-graph-delivery-estimate-fields-removed@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20261027T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261027
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261028
SUMMARY:Meta Graph API: Delivery Estimate drops daily_outcomes_curve\, budg
 et_guardrail and estimate_dau
DESCRIPTION:The daily_outcomes_curve\, budget_guardrail and estimate_dau fi
 elds are removed from GET /{ad-account-id}/delivery_estimate and GET /{ads
 et-id}/delivery_estimate responses because the service behind them was shu
 t down. The removal applies to Marketing API v26.0 and to all remaining ve
 rsions on 2026-10-27\; the calls still succeed but the fields are missing.
 \n\nWhat to do: Stop requesting and reading daily_outcomes_curve\, budget_
 guardrail and estimate_dau\; treat them as absent. Meta offers no replacem
 ent\, so remove any forecasting or budget UI that depends on them or deriv
 e it from the remaining estimate fields.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/meta-graph-delivery-estimate-fields-remove
 d
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:meta-graph-root-ids-lookup-removed@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20261027T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261027
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261028
SUMMARY:Meta Graph API: Root GET /?ids= multi-object lookup returns an erro
 r from 2026-10-27
DESCRIPTION:Graph API dropped legacy protocol features: root requests of th
 e form GET /?ids=a\,b (or /{version}/?ids=) return an error on v26.0+ sinc
 e 2026-07-29 and on all supported versions from 2026-10-27. Meta does not 
 state the error code.\n\nWhat to do: Replace each GET /?ids=... call with 
 one request per object\, or send the per-object requests in a single batch
  request (POST / with a batch parameter)\, and merge the results in your c
 ode.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/meta-graph-root-ids-lookup-removed
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:shopify-global-catalog-rest-api-shutdown@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20261102T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261102
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261103
SUMMARY:Shopify: Shopify Global Catalog REST API stops serving traffic on 2
 026-11-02
DESCRIPTION:The Global Catalog REST API on discover.shopifyapps.com (/globa
 l/v2/search\, /global/v2/p/{upid}\, /global/v2/p/by-variant/{vid}\, POST /
 global/v2/lookup\, including saved-catalog requests) stops serving traffic
  on November 2\, 2026\, and requests to it will fail. Anything still calli
 ng it must move to the Global Catalog MCP server.\n\nWhat to do: Switch to
  the Global Catalog MCP server at https://catalog.shopify.com/api/ucp/mcp:
  use the search_catalog tool instead of GET /global/v2/search\, get_produc
 t instead of the single-product and by-variant lookups\, and lookup_catalo
 g (up to 50 items per request) instead of POST /global/v2/lookup.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/shopify-global-catalog-rest-api-shutdown
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:xero-nz-payroll-employee-tax-kiwisaverstatus-required@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20261105T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261105
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261106
SUMMARY:Xero: NZ Payroll employee tax requests without KiwiSaverStatus retu
 rn 400 from 2026-11-05
DESCRIPTION:From 2026-11-05\, KiwiSaverStatus is required when creating or 
 updating employee tax details in NZ Payroll\, for every tax code except WT
  and NSW. Requests that omit it return 400 Bad Request. Xero says it will 
 not provide test instances or workarounds.\n\nWhat to do: Send KiwiSaverSt
 atus explicitly in every POST to /payroll.xro/2.0/Employees/{EmployeeID}/T
 ax whose tax code is not WT or NSW. Get it from your own employee record o
 r read the current tax details with a GET before updating. Treat a 400 on 
 this call as a data error to show the user\, not a reason to retry.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/xero-nz-payroll-employee-tax-kiwisaverstat
 us-required
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:meta-graph-marketing-api-v24-sunset@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20261110T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261110
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261111
SUMMARY:Meta Graph API: Marketing API v24.0 available until 2026-11-10
DESCRIPTION:Marketing API v24.0 is available until 2026-11-10\, much earlie
 r than Graph API v24.0. After that\, ads calls pinned to v24.0 either fail
  or are auto-upgraded to the next version\; endpoints that changed between
  versions fail. This matches ad account edges (/v24.0/act_{id}/...)\; call
 s to campaign\, ad set and ad objects by numeric id on v24.0 are affected 
 too but cannot be told apart from other Graph calls by path.\n\nWhat to do
 : Move all Marketing API calls (ad accounts\, campaigns\, ad sets\, ads\, 
 creatives\, insights) to v25.0 or\, better\, v26.0\, and re-test against t
 he v25.0 and v26.0 changelogs (for example the Advantage+ campaign and tar
 geting_automation changes) before 2026-11-10.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/meta-graph-marketing-api-v24-sunset
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:google-gemini-2-5-preview-tts-shutdown@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20261117T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261117
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261118
SUMMARY:Google Gemini API: Gemini 2.5 preview TTS models shut down on 2026-
 11-17
DESCRIPTION:Google shuts down gemini-2.5-flash-preview-tts and gemini-2.5-p
 ro-preview-tts on 2026-11-17. After that the models are turned off and spe
 ech-generation calls that name them in the path fail. Calls that pass the 
 model in a request body are not matched by this path.\n\nWhat to do: Switc
 h to gemini-3.8-flash-tts or gemini-3.8-flash-lite-tts before 2026-11-17\;
  the current speech-generation docs send the model in the body of POST /v1
 beta/interactions. Re-check voice names and how you decode the returned au
 dio.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/google-gemini-2-5-preview-tts-shutdown
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:google-gemini-2-5-preview-tts-shutdown-sdk@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20261117T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261117
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261118
SUMMARY:Google Gemini API: Gemini 2.5 preview TTS models shut down on 2026-
 11-17 (model in the request body)
DESCRIPTION:Google shuts down gemini-2.5-flash-preview-tts and gemini-2.5-p
 ro-preview-tts on 2026-11-17. After that the models are turned off and spe
 ech-generation calls that name them fail. This advisory covers calls that 
 pass the model as a parameter\, as the @google/genai SDK does (ai.models.g
 enerateContent({ model }))\; google-gemini-2-5-preview-tts-shutdown covers
  calls that name the model in the path.\n\nWhat to do: Switch to gemini-3.
 8-flash-tts or gemini-3.8-flash-lite-tts before 2026-11-17\; the current s
 peech-generation docs send the model in the body of POST /v1beta/interacti
 ons. Re-check voice names and how you decode the returned audio.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/google-gemini-2-5-preview-tts-shutdown-sdk
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:anthropic-claude-sonnet-4-5-retirement@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20261130T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261130
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261201
SUMMARY:Anthropic: Claude Sonnet 4.5 retires on 2026-11-30
DESCRIPTION:Anthropic retires claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929 on the Claude API 
 on 2026-11-30 (announced 2026-09-30). Only calls that send this model are 
 hit\; requests to a retired model fail.\n\nWhat to do: Change the model to
  claude-sonnet-5-5 (Anthropic's recommended replacement) and follow the So
 nnet 4.5 to 5.5 migration guide\, because some request shapes Sonnet 4.5 a
 ccepts (for example sampling parameters or forced tool use) can return 400
  on newer models. Amazon Bedrock and Google-managed Google Cloud set their
  own retirement dates.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/anthropic-claude-sonnet-4-5-retirement
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:openai-evals-api-shutdown@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20261130T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261130
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261201
SUMMARY:OpenAI: Evals API shuts down on 2026-11-30
DESCRIPTION:OpenAI is retiring the Evals platform: existing evals become re
 ad-only on 2026-10-31\, and the Evals dashboard and API shut down on 2026-
 11-30. After that\, calls to /v1/evals and its runs fail.\n\nWhat to do: E
 xport the eval definitions and results you need before 2026-11-30\, stop c
 reating or updating evals (they are read-only from 2026-10-31)\, and move 
 eval runs to Promptfoo following OpenAI's "Moving from OpenAI Evals to Pro
 mptfoo" guide.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/openai-evals-api-shutdown
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:salesforce-soap-login-use-any-api-auth-required@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20261201T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261202
SUMMARY:Salesforce: SOAP login() requires the Use Any API Auth permission f
 rom 2026-12-01
DESCRIPTION:Salesforce enforces a new control on SOAP API login() in all or
 gs on 2026-12-01: login() succeeds only for users with the Use Any API Aut
 h user permission\, and otherwise is rejected with INSUFFICIENT_ACCESS. It
  is already the default in new orgs. It applies to login() on the Enterpri
 se (/services/Soap/c/{v}) and Partner (/services/Soap/u/{v}) endpoints in 
 API 31.0-64.0\; login() is already unavailable in 65.0 and later.\n\nWhat 
 to do: Assign the Use Any API Auth permission (permission set or profile) 
 to every integration user that still calls SOAP login()\, and test with th
 e 'Assign Use Any API Auth Permission for SOAP login()' release update. Pl
 an the real fix at the same time: authenticate through an External Client 
 App with OAuth 2.0 (JWT bearer or client credentials for server-to-server\
 , web server flow for user-driven apps)\, because login() is retired in Su
 mmer '27.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/salesforce-soap-login-use-any-api-auth-req
 uired
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:hubspot-pipelines-v1-sunset@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20261204T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261204
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261205
SUMMARY:HubSpot: Pipelines API v1 retired on 2026-12-04
DESCRIPTION:HubSpot retires the legacy CRM Pipelines API v1 on 2026-12-04\;
  after that\, calls to v1 endpoints stop working. The replacement is the P
 ipelines API 2026-09 version (GA 2026-09-09). The /crm-pipelines/v1 path c
 omes from HubSpot's legacy v1 reference\; the notice itself names no paths
 .\n\nWhat to do: Call GET /crm/pipelines/2026-09/{objectType} (HubSpot's O
 penAPI spec for the 2026-09 Pipelines API) instead of /crm-pipelines/v1/pi
 pelines/{objectType} before 2026-12-04. The response keeps results[] and s
 tages[]\, but pipelines and stages are identified by id instead of pipelin
 eId and stageId.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/hubspot-pipelines-v1-sunset
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:salesforce-soap-login-broad-ip-range-token-required@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20261215T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261215
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261216
SUMMARY:Salesforce: SOAP login() from a broad IP range needs a security tok
 en from 2026-12-15
DESCRIPTION:Starting 2026-12-15 in sandboxes and 2027-01-31 in production\,
  SOAP API login() for a user whose org or profile login IP range is broad 
 (larger than /8 IPv4 or /29 IPv6) fails without a security token (or mTLS)
 \; username and password alone fail with TOKEN_REQUIRED (Login History res
 ult 1502). It applies to login() on /services/Soap/c/{v} and /services/Soa
 p/u/{v} in API 31.0-64.0.\n\nWhat to do: Preferably switch the integration
  to an External Client App with OAuth 2.0 before 2026-12-15 (sandbox) / 20
 27-01-31 (production). As a stopgap\, append the user's security token to 
 the password in the login() call\, or narrow the org Network Access or pro
 file Login IP Ranges so they are no longer broad\; test with the 'SOAP API
  login() Security Remediation' release update.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/salesforce-soap-login-broad-ip-range-token
 -required
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:salesforce-soap-login-disabled-when-unused@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20261215T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261215
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261216
SUMMARY:Salesforce: SOAP login() turned off in orgs with no use in six mont
 hs\, from 2026-12-15
DESCRIPTION:In a one-time check on 2026-12-15 (sandboxes) and 2027-01-31 (p
 roduction)\, Salesforce disables SOAP API login() in orgs that had no SOAP
  login() call in the previous six months\; after that\, login() fails in t
 hat org. Rarely run jobs (annual\, seasonal\, disaster recovery) can look 
 inactive and then break. One call by any user in the window keeps login() 
 on.\n\nWhat to do: Check Login History (API Type SOAP Enterprise/Partner) 
 and the API Total Usage event log (API_FAMILY SOAP\, API_RESOURCE login) f
 or every integration that uses SOAP login()\, including rarely run jobs\, 
 and move them to an External Client App with OAuth 2.0 before 2026-12-15 (
 sandbox) / 2027-01-31 (production).
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/salesforce-soap-login-disabled-when-unused
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:google-custom-search-json-api-shutdown@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20270101T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270102
SUMMARY:Google APIs: Custom Search JSON API discontinued on 2027-01-01
DESCRIPTION:The Custom Search JSON API is closed to new customers\, and exi
 sting customers have until 2027-01-01 to move off it\; Google calls that d
 ate the service discontinuation. After that\, calls to /customsearch/v1 st
 op working.\n\nWhat to do: Replace calls to www.googleapis.com/customsearc
 h/v1 before 2027-01-01: Google points to Vertex AI Search for searching up
  to 50 domains\, and to its interest form for full-web search. Expect a di
 fferent request format\, response shape and pricing.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/google-custom-search-json-api-shutdown
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:shopify-automatic-discounts-query-removed@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20270101T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270102
SUMMARY:Shopify: Shopify removes the automaticDiscounts query in API versio
 n 2027-01
DESCRIPTION:As of Admin API version 2027-01\, the deprecated automaticDisco
 unts query no longer exists on QueryRoot\, and requests that include it re
 turn a validation error. DiscountAutomaticConnection and DiscountAutomatic
 Edge are removed too.\n\nWhat to do: Query discountNodes with query: "meth
 od:automatic" and read each discount from the discount field. Don't move t
 o automaticDiscountNodes\, which is also deprecated.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/shopify-automatic-discounts-query-removed
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:shopify-collection-metafield-integer-condition-removed@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20270101T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270102
SUMMARY:Shopify: Shopify removes the metafieldInteger collection condition 
 in API version 2027-01
DESCRIPTION:As of Admin API version 2027-01\, the metafieldInteger collecti
 on source condition inputs and types are removed and replaced by metafield
 Int\, whose value is a String instead of an Int.\n\nWhat to do: Before mov
 ing to 2027-01\, replace metafieldInteger with metafieldInt in collection 
 condition inputs and reads (CollectionSourceInclusionConditionMetafieldInt
 )\, and send the value as a String.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/shopify-collection-metafield-integer-condi
 tion-removed
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:shopify-market-currency-settings-update-removed@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20270101T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270102
SUMMARY:Shopify: Shopify removes the marketCurrencySettingsUpdate mutation 
 in API version 2027-01
DESCRIPTION:As of Admin API version 2027-01\, the marketCurrencySettingsUpd
 ate mutation and its payload and error types are removed. Every call alrea
 dy returns the UNIFIED_MARKETS_ENABLED user error\; on 2027-01 the request
  is rejected at validation.\n\nWhat to do: Set market currency settings th
 rough marketCreate and marketUpdate\, which accept them directly\, and rem
 ove calls to marketCurrencySettingsUpdate before moving to 2027-01.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/shopify-market-currency-settings-update-re
 moved
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:shopify-metaobject-admin-access-private-public-read-removed@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20270101T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270102
SUMMARY:Shopify: Shopify deprecates the PRIVATE and PUBLIC_READ metaobject 
 admin access values
DESCRIPTION:The PRIVATE and PUBLIC_READ values of the MetaobjectAdminAccess
  enum are deprecated and are never returned by the API\; they go away with
  API version 2027-01.\n\nWhat to do: Stop sending PRIVATE or PUBLIC_READ a
 s a metaobject definition's admin access\, and drop code that expects them
  back.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/shopify-metaobject-admin-access-private-pu
 blic-read-removed
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:shopify-non-expiring-offline-tokens-rejected@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20270101T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270102
SUMMARY:Shopify: Shopify rejects non-expiring offline access tokens from pu
 blic apps on 2027-01-01
DESCRIPTION:Starting January 1\, 2027\, every public app (including ones cr
 eated before April 1\, 2026) must use expiring offline access tokens to ca
 ll the Admin API. Shopify enforces this on GraphQL Admin API requests: a r
 equest with a non-expiring token gets 403 Forbidden with "Non-expiring acc
 ess tokens are no longer accepted for the Admin API"\, and merchants lose 
 access until they re-authenticate. Custom apps and merchant-created apps a
 re not affected.\n\nWhat to do: Exchange each stored non-expiring token fo
 r an expiring one with POST /admin/oauth/access_token (grant_type=urn:ietf
 :params:oauth:grant-type:token-exchange\, subject_token_type and requested
 _token_type urn:shopify:params:oauth:token-type:offline-access-token\, exp
 iring=1)\, store the access token\, refresh token and expiry\, and refresh
  before expiry\; on the official app templates set future.expiringOfflineA
 ccessTokens: true and redeploy. Check API Health in the Dev Dashboard to c
 onfirm the app is migrated.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/shopify-non-expiring-offline-tokens-reject
 ed
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:shopify-tax-managed-mode-write-validation@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20270101T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270102
SUMMARY:Shopify: Shopify Tax managed mode rejects market and publishing wri
 tes that conflict with it
DESCRIPTION:For stores using Shopify Tax managed mode\, Markets API writes 
 and product publishing writes can now fail validation when they conflict w
 ith managed-mode requirements\, and the taxable input on custom line items
  is deprecated in favor of productCategoryId.\n\nWhat to do: Handle valida
 tion errors from marketCreate\, marketUpdate and publishablePublish for st
 ores in Shopify Tax managed mode\, and omit tax settings your app doesn't 
 need to manage. For custom line items\, send productCategoryId instead of 
 taxable.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/shopify-tax-managed-mode-write-validation
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:openai-gpt-4o-gpt-4-1-snapshots-shutdown-2027-01-14@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20270114T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270114
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270115
SUMMARY:OpenAI: gpt-4o\, gpt-4o-mini\, gpt-4.1 and gpt-4.1-mini snapshots s
 hut down on 2027-01-14
DESCRIPTION:OpenAI shuts down gpt-4o-2024-08-06\, gpt-4o-2024-11-20\, gpt-4
 o-mini-2024-07-18\, gpt-4.1-2025-04-14 and gpt-4.1-mini-2025-04-14 on 2027
 -01-14\, and fine-tunes of these models follow the same date. Only calls t
 hat send one of these models are hit. The notice lists dated snapshots and
  does not say what happens to the undated gpt-4o or gpt-4o-mini aliases.\n
 \nWhat to do: Replace these model names with gpt-6-luna (OpenAI's recommen
 ded replacement) in request bodies and config\, re-run fine-tunes on a sup
 ported base model\, and compare output quality before 2027-01-14. The same
  model names are also used on the Responses API.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/openai-gpt-4o-gpt-4-1-snapshots-shutdown-2
 027-01-14
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:openai-gpt-4o-gpt-4-1-snapshots-shutdown-2027-01-14-responses@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20270114T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270114
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270115
SUMMARY:OpenAI: gpt-4o\, gpt-4o-mini\, gpt-4.1 and gpt-4.1-mini snapshots s
 hut down on 2027-01-14 (Responses API)
DESCRIPTION:OpenAI shuts down gpt-4o-2024-08-06\, gpt-4o-2024-11-20\, gpt-4
 o-mini-2024-07-18\, gpt-4.1-2025-04-14 and gpt-4.1-mini-2025-04-14 on 2027
 -01-14\, and fine-tunes of these models follow the same date. This advisor
 y covers calls to the Responses API (POST /v1/responses) that send one of 
 these models\; openai-gpt-4o-gpt-4-1-snapshots-shutdown-2027-01-14 covers 
 chat completions. The notice lists dated snapshots and does not say what h
 appens to the undated gpt-4o or gpt-4o-mini aliases.\n\nWhat to do: Replac
 e these model names with gpt-6-luna (OpenAI's recommended replacement) in 
 request bodies and config\, re-run fine-tunes on a supported base model\, 
 and compare output quality before 2027-01-14. The same model names are als
 o used on the Responses API.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/openai-gpt-4o-gpt-4-1-snapshots-shutdown-2
 027-01-14-responses
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:xero-invoices-email-daily-limit-429@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20270114T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270114
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270115
SUMMARY:Xero: Invoice email daily limit returns 429 instead of 500 from 202
 7-01-14
DESCRIPTION:From 2027-01-14\, POST Invoices/{InvoiceID}/Email returns 429 T
 oo Many Requests instead of a generic 500 when the organisation reaches it
 s daily invoice-email limit. The 429 has no Retry-After header. Code that 
 treats 500 as a retryable server error\, or retries a 429 at once with a s
 hort backoff\, will mishandle the limit.\n\nWhat to do: Handle a 429 from 
 the invoice Email endpoint separately from the per-minute rate limit. It i
 s a daily limit with no Retry-After header\, so don't retry immediately. Q
 ueue the send for after the daily reset\, or tell the user sending was del
 ayed. Stop relying on a 500 to detect this case.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/xero-invoices-email-daily-limit-429
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:shopify-admin-api-2026-01-unsupported@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20270116T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270116
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270117
SUMMARY:Shopify: Shopify Admin API version 2026-01 becomes unsupported on 2
 027-01-16
DESCRIPTION:Admin API version 2026-01 is accessible until January 16\, 2027
  15:00 UTC. After that\, requests to /admin/api/2026-01/... (REST and Grap
 hQL) and webhooks pinned to 2026-01 fall forward to the oldest accessible 
 stable version without an error\, so responses can change shape silently. 
 Every app still pinned to 2026-01 is hit.\n\nWhat to do: Move the version 
 segment in your Admin API URLs and webhook subscriptions to a supported ve
 rsion (2026-04 or later\; 2026-10 is the latest stable)\, work through the
  release notes for every version in between\, and check the X-Shopify-API-
 Version response header to confirm Shopify is not falling forward.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/shopify-admin-api-2026-01-unsupported
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:meta-graph-v21-sunset@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20270121T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270121
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270122
SUMMARY:Meta Graph API: Graph API v21.0 removed on 2027-01-21
DESCRIPTION:Graph API v21.0 is deprecated and removed on 2027-01-21. After 
 that\, calls pinned to v21.0 are served by the next oldest usable version 
 without an error.\n\nWhat to do: Move the version segment to a supported v
 ersion (v22.0 or later) and re-test the fields you read.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/meta-graph-v21-sunset
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:twilio-notify-end-of-life@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20270131T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270131
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270201
SUMMARY:Twilio: Twilio Notify reaches end of life on 2027-01-31
DESCRIPTION:Twilio Notify (notify.twilio.com\, e.g. POST /v1/Services/{Serv
 iceSid}/Notifications) has been unsupported and closed to new customers si
 nce October 2022 and reaches end of life for existing customers on 2027-01
 -31\, per Twilio's Help Center (superseding the 2025-12-31 date in the Jan
 uary 2024 changelog). Push sent through Verify\, Voice\, Conversations or 
 Engage is not affected.\n\nWhat to do: Move bulk SMS sends to the Messagin
 g API (or Twilio's Bulk Messaging API) and push notifications to a direct 
 APNs/FCM integration or another push provider\, then remove Notify Service
 s and Bindings.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/twilio-notify-end-of-life
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quickbooks-refresh-token-five-year-hard-expiry@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20270201T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270202
SUMMARY:QuickBooks Online: Refresh tokens hard-expire after five years\, fi
 rst ones in February 2027
DESCRIPTION:Intuit refresh tokens now have a maximum lifetime of five years
 \, even if they are used regularly. For apps on restricted or granular sco
 pes\, tokens issued from February 2022 start expiring in February 2027. Fo
 r com.intuit.quickbooks.accounting and com.intuit.quickbooks.payments\, to
 kens issued from October 2023 start expiring in October 2028. Intuit gives
  only the month\, so the effective date here is the first day of that mont
 h.\n\nWhat to do: On token requests\, send the header x-include-refresh-to
 ken-hard-expires-in: true (Intuit's docs also list an x_refresh_token_hard
 _expires_in=true parameter) and store the returned x_refresh_token_hard_ex
 pires_in (seconds left in the five-year lifetime) alongside the token. Tre
 at invalid_grant from /oauth2/v1/tokens/bearer as a disconnect that needs 
 the user to reconnect\, not as a retryable error. Prompt users to re-autho
 rize before the hard expiry\, and set the Reconnect URL in the developer p
 ortal app settings.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/quickbooks-refresh-token-five-year-hard-ex
 piry
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:meta-graph-marketing-api-v25-sunset@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20270223T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270223
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270224
SUMMARY:Meta Graph API: Marketing API v25.0 available until 2027-02-23
DESCRIPTION:Marketing API v25.0 is available until 2027-02-23 (Graph API v2
 5.0 itself runs to 2028). After that\, ads calls pinned to v25.0 fail or a
 re auto-upgraded\, and endpoints that changed in v26.0 fail. Meta also say
 s the explicit targeting_automation.advantage_audience flag becomes mandat
 ory on all versions once v25.0 is deprecated.\n\nWhat to do: Upgrade Marke
 ting API calls to v26.0\, set targeting_automation.advantage_audience to 1
  or 0 explicitly on ad set targeting\, and review the v26.0 changelog (pol
 l ads\, Messenger Stories\, Explore placement\, delivery estimate fields) 
 before 2027-02-23.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/meta-graph-marketing-api-v25-sunset
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:openai-audio-translations-endpoint-shutdown@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20270226T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270226
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270227
SUMMARY:OpenAI: /v1/audio/translations shuts down on 2027-02-26
DESCRIPTION:OpenAI deprecated the audio translations endpoint on 2026-08-26
  and shuts it down on 2027-02-26\, together with whisper-1 and the gpt-4o 
 transcribe models. After that date every call to POST /v1/audio/translatio
 ns fails.\n\nWhat to do: Replace calls to POST /v1/audio/translations with
  the Realtime translations interface (v1/realtime/translations) that OpenA
 I names as the replacement\, and move transcription off whisper-1 to gpt-l
 ive-transcribe or gpt-transcribe before 2027-02-26.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/openai-audio-translations-endpoint-shutdow
 n
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:shopify-script-tags-stop-running@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20270301T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270301
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270302
SUMMARY:Shopify: Shopify script tags stop running on storefronts on 2027-03
 -01
DESCRIPTION:Script tags are deprecated in every Admin API version. Since Oc
 tober 1\, 2026 the REST ScriptTag resource rejects POST and PUT and the Gr
 aphQL scriptTagCreate and scriptTagUpdate mutations return a user error\; 
 on March 1\, 2027 Shopify stops injecting existing script tags into storef
 ronts\, so their JavaScript no longer loads. Listing and deleting script t
 ags keeps working.\n\nWhat to do: Stop creating or updating script tags (P
 OST /admin/api/{version}/script_tags.json and PUT .../script_tags/{script_
 tag_id}.json already fail). Move storefront scripts to app embed blocks in
  a theme app extension\, and analytics or conversion scripts to a web pixe
 l\; then delete the old script tags. Pinning an older API version does not
  delay this.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/shopify-script-tags-stop-running
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:google-gemini-2-5-flash-image-shutdown@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20270315T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270315
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270316
SUMMARY:Google Gemini API: gemini-2.5-flash-image shuts down on 2027-03-15
DESCRIPTION:Google shuts down gemini-2.5-flash-image (the original Nano Ban
 ana image model) on 2027-03-15. After that the model is turned off and gen
 erateContent calls that name it in the path fail. Calls that pass the mode
 l in a request body are not matched by this path.\n\nWhat to do: Move imag
 e generation to gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image\, the replacement on the depre
 cations page\, before 2027-03-15\, and re-test how you read the returned i
 mage parts.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/google-gemini-2-5-flash-image-shutdown
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:google-gemini-2-5-flash-image-shutdown-sdk@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20270315T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270315
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270316
SUMMARY:Google Gemini API: gemini-2.5-flash-image shuts down on 2027-03-15 
 (model in the request body)
DESCRIPTION:Google shuts down gemini-2.5-flash-image (the original Nano Ban
 ana image model) on 2027-03-15. After that the model is turned off and gen
 erateContent calls that name it fail. This advisory covers calls that pass
  the model as a parameter\, as the @google/genai SDK does (ai.models.gener
 ateContent({ model }))\; google-gemini-2-5-flash-image-shutdown covers cal
 ls that name the model in the path.\n\nWhat to do: Move image generation t
 o gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image\, the replacement on the deprecations page\,
  before 2027-03-15\, and re-test how you read the returned image parts.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/google-gemini-2-5-flash-image-shutdown-sdk
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:shopify-admin-api-2026-04-unsupported@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20270416T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270416
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270417
SUMMARY:Shopify: Shopify Admin API version 2026-04 becomes unsupported on 2
 027-04-16
DESCRIPTION:Admin API version 2026-04 is accessible until April 16\, 2027 1
 5:00 UTC. After that\, requests to /admin/api/2026-04/... (REST and GraphQ
 L) and webhooks pinned to 2026-04 fall forward to the oldest accessible st
 able version without an error\, so responses can change shape silently. Ev
 ery app still pinned to 2026-04 is hit.\n\nWhat to do: Move the version se
 gment in your Admin API URLs and webhook subscriptions to a supported vers
 ion (2026-07 or later\; 2026-10 is the latest stable)\, work through the r
 elease notes for every version in between\, and check the X-Shopify-API-Ve
 rsion response header to confirm Shopify is not falling forward.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/shopify-admin-api-2026-04-unsupported
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:xero-accounting-transactions-scope-split@shapi.dev
DTSTAMP:20270913T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270913
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270914
SUMMARY:Xero: Broad accounting.transactions scope replaced by granular scop
 es
DESCRIPTION:Xero split accounting.transactions into granular scopes (invoic
 es\, payments\, bank transactions\, manual journals\, classic expenses\, e
 ach with a .read variant). Apps created after 2026-03-02 must request gran
 ular scopes\; existing apps keep the broad scopes until September 2027\, a
 nd each connected user must re-authorize to receive the new ones.\n\nWhat 
 to do: Request the granular scopes in the authorization URL and have each 
 connection re-authorize before the cutoff.
URL:https://shapi.dev/advisories/xero-accounting-transactions-scope-split
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
